styles='code,a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.card{min-width:0}body{margin:0;background:#f6f5ef;color:#233f35;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px}h1{font:40px/1.15 Georgia,serif}h2{margin-top:36px;line-height:1.3}a{color:#245d41}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white;font-size:14px}th,td{border:1px solid #d5dfd4;padding:12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#e7eee4}.scroll{overflow:auto}.notice{padding:18px;border-left:4px solid #9b783e;background:#eee6d4}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #d5dfd4;border-radius:12px;padding:20px}.value{display:block;font-size:30px;font-weight:600}label{display:block;margin:12px 0}input,select,button{font:inherit;padding:8px;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}input[type=number]{width:130px}input[type=checkbox]{width:auto}button{cursor:pointer;background:#284e3b;color:white;border:0;border-radius:6px;margin:5px}.muted{color:#596b61}li{margin:10px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:24px 16px}h1{font-size:32px}.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.scroll table{min-width:680px}}'
rows=''.join(f"<tr><td>{x['registered']:,}</td><td>{x['mau']:,}</td><td>{x['storageGB']:.3f} GB</td><td>{x['databaseGB']:.3f} GB</td><td>{x['uncachedEgressGB']:.2f} GB</td><td>{x['emailsPerMonth']:,}</td><td>{x['netlifyCredits']:.0f}</td><td>${x['estimatedMonthlyUSD']:g}</td></tr>" for x in model['scenarios'])
body='''<p>READINESS REVIEW - 14 NOVEMBER 2026</p><h1>Cost controls: locally verified, hosted launch still blocked.</h1>
<p class="notice"><strong>No hosted services were changed, enabled or deployed.</strong> The Netlify image-function candidate and application changes were validated locally. This does not certify Linux/serverless runtime behavior, production permissions, billing configuration or live performance. The root deployment configuration remains unchanged.</p>
<p><a href="MONTHLY-COST-DASHBOARD.html">Open the monthly operating-cost dashboard</a> - <a href="COST-CONTROL-PLAN.html">Previous detailed plan</a> (this review supersedes its hosted-processing status and selected-host cost estimate).</p>
<h2>Verified safeguards</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Hosted-function source is implemented.</strong> <code>deployment/netlify/functions/upload.mjs</code> uses a server-only handler with explicit credentials, exact HTTPS application origin and the intended Supabase project. It returns 503 unless deliberately configured/enabled. No fixture imports or local fallback exist in the deployment entry. A separate candidate TOML describes function bundling and routing; it is not active.</li>
<li><strong>Browser preparation is not trusted.</strong> Files over 4 MB and within the existing 8 MiB selection limit are prepared in the browser. A generated 5.9 MB PNG was successfully reduced below the transport limit. The function independently counts streamed bytes, rejects requests above 4,000,000 bytes (below Netlify's effective ~4.5 MB binary limit), validates authenticated ownership through existing RPCs and decodes the actual image bytes.</li>
<li><strong>Trusted compression remains mandatory.</strong> JPEG, PNG and WebP still images only; 25 MP decode guard; EXIF removed; image maximum 1600 px and 450 KB, thumbnail maximum 400 px and 50 KB. Complex images reduce dimensions/quality; unsupported or uncompressible files fail. Only these optimized outputs enter the private bucket.</li>
<li><strong>Only the worker finalizes.</strong> Ordinary users cannot write directly to Storage or call privileged finalization. Finalization rechecks current ownership and membership. Wrong-origin, invalid bearer, cross-family destinations, spoofed content, malformed bytes and oversized requests are rejected. Partial-write failure removes the newly written image; a failed deletion keeps capacity reserved for cleanup.</li>
<li><strong>Quota reservations now survive content deletion.</strong> A new private database ledger closes the cancellation/in-flight race. Its records are inaccessible to browser roles. Concurrent requests across different accounts cannot take the last available slot twice. The 50 MB account cap, 20 daily reservations, global 800 MB cap and 500 KB finalization limit remain.</li>
</ul>
<p>Evidence: <a href="output/cost-readiness/hosted-handler-tests.json">11 hosted-handler/local-database scenarios</a>, <a href="output/cost-readiness/transport-test.json">large-file browser transport</a>, <a href="output/cost-controls/database-tests.json">6 quota checks</a>. The function bundle was built locally with server dependencies external. The native Sharp package must be installed for Linux by the future hosting build; this Windows run cannot validate that deployment binary.</p>
<h2>What happens at 800 MB</h2>
<p>The budget is <strong>800,000,000 bytes (decimal MB)</strong>, not 800 MiB. A request must fit another 500,000-byte reservation in addition to recorded storage bytes and outstanding reservations. It can therefore stop slightly before exactly 800 MB. Pending uploads may temporarily be double-counted while their stored objects exist but finalization is unfinished; this is deliberately conservative.</p>
<ol><li>Reservation fails before decoding or writing a new object. The hosted handler returns HTTP 429 with <em>Photo storage is nearly full. New uploads are paused until space is available.</em> The existing upload UI displays that error.</li><li>Existing photos are neither modified nor deleted. Authorized downloads still succeed; unauthorized downloads still fail. Family records, messages, text posts and sign-in are not disabled by this photo-specific cap.</li><li>In-flight uploads with valid reservations can finish. Deleting their parent content cannot release the reserved space early; finalization then fails authorization and the new objects are cleaned up.</li><li>Capacity can return after actual orphan bytes are removed, or a canceled reservation expires after one day. Deleting a photo in the UI revokes access immediately but may not reclaim stored bytes until maintenance runs. The current local maintenance runs hourly and processes at most 500 orphan paths per batch; hosted maintenance remains unconfigured.</li><li>A local full-capacity test preserved reads, created no new storage object, and resumed uploads after synthetic capacity was freed. No real hosted storage was filled.</li></ol>
<p class="notice">The cap protects the application workflow, not a compromised service-role key or manual administrator upload. It is project-local and includes all its recorded Storage objects; it does not cap other projects in the billing organization. Unknown or malformed object-size metadata now pauses new reservations rather than treating those bytes as zero. Provider ingestion/accounting lag still requires dashboard reconciliation. No claim of absolute provider billing enforcement is made.</p>
<h2>Provider verification: policies versus your actual accounts</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Verified public behavior</th><th>Actual account status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Free: no usage charges, but quotas/restrictions apply. Pro Spend Cap covers certain usage meters; compute, extra projects/branches, replicas, PITR and other opt-in add-ons are excluded. It is not a custom dollar cap or threshold notification system.</td><td><strong>Plan, cap, add-ons and billing recipients unverified.</strong> A fresh read-only Auth configuration check confirms custom SMTP is absent, site URL remains localhost, redirect allowlist empty, email rate 2/hour. No account records or settings were changed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Resend</td><td>Free: 3,000 emails/month, 100/day. Paid Transactional Overages is an explicit setting; when enabled it bills additional 1,000-email buckets. Provider documentation describes usage alerts at 80% and 100%. Sending and receiving both consume quota.</td><td><strong>Account/plan, Transactional Overages, sender domain and alert recipients unverified.</strong> No connected tool, credential or dashboard session available. Supabase SMTP is not configured; do not infer a Resend account exists. Free quota exhaustion may block verification emails.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Netlify (selected candidate)</td><td>Credit-based Free: 300 credits/month with a hard limit and no recharge option. Paid plans support optional auto-recharge; disabling recharge does not eliminate the base subscription. Production deploys, traffic, previews and function compute consume shared credits.</td><td><strong>Actual team/site, plan generation, auto-recharge and alerts unverified.</strong> No linked .netlify/state.json, CLI/environment credential or browser session was found. The repository's Netlify configuration selects the implementation target, not proof of an existing hosted site.</td></tr></table></div>
<p>Read-only access evidence and Auth settings: <a href="output/cost-readiness/provider-review.json">provider review</a>. Browser access returned unavailable, and connector discovery found no usable Netlify/Resend billing tool. No dashboard settings were changed. These rows remain deployment blockers; a public pricing page cannot verify your subscriptions.</p>
<h2>Validated assumptions and revised estimates</h2>
<p>Measured 8 local fixture portraits: combined outputs 14-152 KB, average about 61 KB, with local processing roughly 0.10-0.36 seconds. These are small fixture images, not a production distribution or serverless benchmark. Keep a conservative <strong>180 KB average</strong>, a 500 KB worst-case bound, and a provisional 1 GB-second worker allowance per upload until measured on the selected runtime.</p>
<p>Baseline: 20% of registered accounts monthly active; 2 photos/active user/month; 12 months accumulated content; profile photos for 40% of registered accounts. Bandwidth: 120 photo views/active user/month, 70% at 20 KB thumbnails and 30% at 180 KB full images, plus 3 MB API/chat traffic: <strong>11.16 MB per MAU/month</strong>. Static app: 4 sessions/MAU/month, 2 MB and 20 requests/session. Emails: 2 per MAU plus new registrations equal to 5% of registered accounts; retries and onboarding bursts are extra.</p>
<p>Database planning: 70 MB baseline +20 KB/account +103 KB/MAU/month for 50 messages, 2 posts, 4 comments and related/index overhead. Local fixture rows average about 81-133 bytes before indexes; small-table physical sizes substantially exceed raw rows. The planning allowances are deliberately higher, but family size, duplicate profiles, long text, indexes and vacuum bloat are not validated at 10,000 users. The database estimate is a planning range, not a capacity proof.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Registered</th><th>MAU</th><th>Photos at month 12</th><th>Database</th><th>Monthly backend egress</th><th>Emails/month</th><th>Netlify credits</th><th>Monthly estimate</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table></div>
<p>The 100-user case fits modeled Free allowances. At 1,000 users, Free can work initially but the application photo ceiling is reached near month 10; $25 reflects a future approved Supabase Pro decision. At 10,000 users, $25 Supabase +$20 Resend +$9 Netlify Personal = <strong>$54/month</strong>. The earlier $45 estimate requires moving static hosting to free Cloudflare hosting, leaving only the small image function allocation on Netlify. That alternative is not selected or implemented by this review. If all 10,000 accounts are monthly active at baseline per-user activity, the selected-host estimate rises to roughly <strong>$65.58/month</strong>, before larger compute or other excluded costs.</p>
<p>At 10,000 registrations, assumed profile photos alone consume 720 MB; there is almost no free photo headroom before active uploads. These populations cannot simply be admitted under the current 800 MB ceiling. A paid plan does not automatically raise the application cap. Both plan and revised quota require separate approval. At a 500 KB average, the 12-month photo estimate is approximately 0.26, 2.6 and 26 GB for the three populations.</p>
<p>Prices are conditional and exclude tax, domain purchase/renewal, independent encrypted backup storage and staff time. Small Supabase compute is assumed; its throughput is unmeasured. No live bill was verified. No messages are automatically emailed; enabling email notifications would materially change this model. The initial 10,000-account onboarding can itself require 10,000 emails, so free daily limits require a staggered rollout or an approved provider plan. Auth MAU and registered users are distinct billing concepts.</p>
<p>Reproduce with <code>node scripts/estimate-readiness.mjs</code>. Sources and measurements: <a href="output/cost-readiness/estimates.json">scenario data</a>, <a href="output/cost-readiness/measurements.json">local measurements</a>. The interactive dashboard exposes the important assumptions without connecting to any provider.</p>
<h2>Commercial operation and free-tier constraints</h2>
<p>Netlify explicitly allows commercial projects on Free. No blanket noncommercial-only restriction was identified for Supabase or Resend in the reviewed pricing/terms; this is a scoped review, not a guarantee about every future business activity or negotiated account agreement. Resend requires a verified sending domain for arbitrary recipients; test-sender restrictions would prevent real-user authentication. Anti-spam/abuse requirements apply, and usage limits are not permission to send unsolicited email.</p>
<p>Practical barriers remain: Free database/storage quotas, inactivity pausing, no automatic Supabase backup entitlement, provider service suspension/fair-use rules, daily email caps, Netlify account-wide credit exhaustion, lack of an SLA, and unverified restoration. These can interrupt a commercial app even without generating a bill. Do not evade quotas with duplicate accounts or weaken privacy/backups to remain free.</p>
<h2>Your manual checks</h2><ol>
<li><strong>Before launch - Supabase:</strong> open the correct organization Billing/Usage pages. Record plan, all projects, base subscription, compute sizes/add-ons, Spend Cap status if Pro, billing recipient and billing-period dates. Confirm total organization usage, not just this project. Do not upgrade or toggle settings during this read-only review.</li>
<li><strong>Before launch - Resend:</strong> confirm whether an account exists, its plan, verified sender/domain, daily/monthly counters, Transactional Overages setting and actual alert recipient. Record quota resets in UTC. Check that native usage notices reach you; do not send a real-user test until separately authorized.</li>
<li><strong>Before launch - Netlify:</strong> identify the team/site, whether pricing is legacy or credit-based, base plan, auto-recharge, add-ons, all sites sharing credits, and billing alert recipients. Target Free/no recharge; any adjustment requires a later authorized change.</li>
<li><strong>Weekly, daily above 70%:</strong> enter measured figures in the dashboard, including Storage bytes, pending reservations, database size, egress, email usage, Realtime usage/connections and Netlify credits. Check invoice estimates against the previous week. Unknown is not zero.</li>
<li><strong>At 90%:</strong> review admissions and discretionary activity before limits interrupt service. Do not delete family content or purchase capacity automatically. At 800 MB, investigate pending/failed uploads and orphan cleanup; preserve existing photos. Allow maintenance to reclaim actual bytes before retrying.</li>
<li><strong>Monthly:</strong> reconcile actual invoices, inspect unexpected add-ons/charges, export the dashboard record, confirm alerts and backup restoration, and update the forecast from real MAU and photo/download averages. Recheck provider pricing before approving any plan change.</li></ol>
<h2>Remaining risks and approval gates</h2>
<p><strong>Still unverified:</strong> live billing settings; Linux Sharp packaging and hosted cold-start/CPU limits; deployed origin/credentials/routing; hostile-traffic edge limits/CAPTCHA; hosted cleanup scheduling; backup restoration; 10,000-user database/Realtime load. The new candidate migration extends the set to 18 files; repeat the entire migration rehearsal/manifest. Existing hosted security findings, including blocked-message history semantics, are not resolved by cost controls.</p>
<p><strong>Requires later approval:</strong> any hosted migration/configuration/deployment, enabling the function/maintenance, configuring SMTP/domain/security settings, accepting provider terms, buying a domain or subscription, raising the 800 MB budget, enabling any overage/recharge, or switching hosting. This review makes none of those changes. Read-only inspection and local testing are complete; hosted launch remains NO-GO until the evidence gaps and security/recovery blockers are resolved.</p>
<h2>Primary references</h2><ul>
<li><a href="https://supabase.com/pricing">Supabase pricing</a>; <a href="https://supabase.com/docs/guides/platform/cost-control">spend-cap coverage</a>; <a href="https://supabase.com/terms">terms</a>.</li>
<li><a href="https://resend.com/pricing">Resend pricing</a>; <a href="https://resend.com/changelog/pay-as-you-go-pricing">overages and usage alerts</a>; <a href="https://resend.com/docs/api-reference/errors">quota/domain restrictions</a>; <a href="https://resend.com/legal/terms-of-service">terms</a>.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.netlify.com/pricing/">Netlify pricing</a>; <a href="https://docs.netlify.com/manage/accounts-and-billing/billing/billing-for-credit-based-plans/configure-auto-recharge/">auto-recharge</a>; <a href="https://docs.netlify.com/build/functions/configuration/">function limits</a>; <a href="https://www.netlify.com/blog/introducing-netlify-free-plan/">commercial use</a>.</li></ul>'''
Path('COST-READINESS-REVIEW.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>FamilyConnect cost readiness review</title><style>'+styles+'</style><main>'+body+'</main></html>',encoding='utf-8')
modeljs=Path('scripts/cost-model.mjs').read_text().replace('export function','function')
fields=[('photos','Photo bytes + pending reservations (MB)',800),('database','Database (MB)',500),('egress','Uncached backend egress (GB)',5),('emailday','Emails today',100),('emailmonth','Emails this month',3000),('realtime','Realtime events this month',2000000),('connections','Peak Realtime connections',200),('credits','Netlify credits',300)]
fieldrows=''.join(f'<tr><td><label for="actual-{key}">{label}</label></td><td><input type="number" min="0" step="any" id="actual-{key}" placeholder="Unknown"></td><td>{limit:,}</td><td id="status-{key}">Unknown</td></tr>' for key,label,limit in fields)
dashboard='''<p>FAMILYCONNECT - MONTHLY OPERATING REVIEW</p><h1>Know the cost before approving growth.</h1><p class="notice">Manual dashboard, not connected billing. Blank values are unknown. Forecasts are not invoices. Saving stores only the values you enter in this browser; no data is sent. <a href="COST-READINESS-REVIEW.html">Read safeguards, risks and manual checks</a>.</p>
<label>Billing month <input id="month" type="month" value="2026-11"></label><label>Provider figures checked on <input id="checked" type="date"></label>
<h2>Actual monthly charges</h2><div class="cards"><label class="card">Supabase USD <input id="bill-supabase" type="number" min="0" step=".01" placeholder="Unknown"></label><label class="card">Resend USD <input id="bill-resend" type="number" min="0" step=".01" placeholder="Unknown"></label><label class="card">Netlify USD <input id="bill-netlify" type="number" min="0" step=".01" placeholder="Unknown"></label></div><p id="bill-total" class="value">Total: not verified</p><p>Enter invoice or current-period provider estimates consistently. Domain, tax and backup costs are additional.</p>
<h2>Usage against the starting free-tier budgets</h2><p>Do not use these thresholds unchanged after a plan approval. Photo budget is the application's 800 MB ceiling; Supabase Free Storage allowance is 1 GB. Figures are decimal MB/GB.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Actual</th><th>Budget</th><th>Status</th></tr>'''+fieldrows+'''</table></div><p id="freshness">Provider figures have not been verified.</p>
<h2>Forecast: selected Netlify hosting</h2><div class="cards"><label class="card">Registered accounts <select id="registered"><option>100</option><option>1000</option><option selected>10000</option></select></label><label class="card">Monthly active percentage <input id="active" type="number" min="1" max="100" value="20"></label><label class="card">Months of accumulated content <input id="months" type="number" min="1" max="36" value="12"></label><label class="card">Photos per active user/month <input id="uploads" type="number" min="1" max="20" value="2"></label><label class="card">Average photo + thumbnail KB <input id="photoKB" type="number" min="10" max="500" value="180"></label><label class="card">Photo views per active user/month <input id="views" type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="120"></label></div>
<p id="forecast" class="value"></p><p id="forecast-details"></p><p id="forecast-warning" class="notice"></p><p>Baseline assumes 70% thumbnail views at 20 KB, 30% full photos, 3 MB other backend traffic/MAU, 4 frontend sessions/MAU at 2 MB each, 50 messages/MAU/month, 2 auth emails/MAU plus 5% new registrations, 1 GB-second/image processing, and four production deploys/month. It is not a load-test guarantee. Excludes tax, domain, independent backup custody and larger compute. Above quoted hosting tiers, obtain a fresh quote.</p>
<h2>Monthly checklist</h2><label><input type="checkbox" id="check-plans"> Recorded actual provider plans, add-ons and billing periods</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="check-caps"> Verified Supabase cap, Resend overages and Netlify recharge settings</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="check-alerts"> Verified billing/usage alert recipients and receipt</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="check-backups"> Checked cleanup and independent backup restoration</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="check-invoices"> Reconciled invoices and forecast; no unapproved purchases</label>
<button id="save">Save this browser's review</button><button id="export">Export review JSON</button><p id="saved" role="status"></p>'''
script=modeljs+'\nconst metrics='+json.dumps(fields)+''';
const all=()=>[...document.querySelectorAll('input,select')];
function update(){
 const charges=['supabase','resend','netlify'].map(k=>document.getElementById('bill-'+k).value);
 document.getElementById('bill-total').textContent=charges.every(v=>v!==''&&Number(v)>=0)?'Entered total: $'+charges.reduce((s,v)=>s+Number(v),0).toFixed(2):'Total: not verified';
 for(const [k,label,limit]of metrics){const v=document.getElementById('actual-'+k).value,n=Number(v);document.getElementById('status-'+k).textContent=v===''||n<0?'Unknown':n>=limit?'LIMIT REACHED':n>=limit*.9?'Critical (90%+)':n>=limit*.7?'Warning (70%+)':'Within entered budget';}
 const date=document.getElementById('checked').value;document.getElementById('freshness').textContent=!date?'Provider figures have not been verified.':Date.now()-Date.parse(date)>48*3600000?'Stale: refresh provider figures before making a spending decision.':'Manually dated figures; provider settings still require inspection.';
 const n=k=>Number(document.getElementById(k).value),valid=['active','months','uploads','photoKB','views'].every(k=>document.getElementById(k).checkValidity()&&document.getElementById(k).value!=='');
 if(!valid){document.getElementById('forecast').textContent='Enter values within the displayed ranges.';document.getElementById('forecast-details').textContent='';return}
 const x=estimate(n('registered'),n('active')/100,{months:n('months'),uploads:n('uploads'),photoKB:n('photoKB'),views:n('views')});
 document.getElementById('forecast').textContent=x.estimatedMonthlyUSD===null?'Hosting quote required':'Modeled monthly services: $'+x.estimatedMonthlyUSD.toFixed(2);
 document.getElementById('forecast-details').textContent=x.mau.toLocaleString()+' monthly active | '+x.storageGB.toFixed(2)+' GB photos | '+x.databaseGB.toFixed(2)+' GB database | '+x.uncachedEgressGB.toFixed(2)+' GB monthly backend egress | '+x.emailsPerMonth.toLocaleString()+' emails/month | '+x.netlifyCredits.toFixed(0)+' Netlify credits';
 document.getElementById('forecast-warning').textContent=(x.storageGB>.8?'Exceeds the current 800 MB app ceiling. Approval is needed before increasing capacity. ':'Photo storage fits the current model ceiling. ')+(x.estimatedMonthlyUSD>0?'Paid plans shown are proposals, not activated subscriptions. ':'Free operation is conditional on verified plans and workload. ')+'The earlier Cloudflare-static alternative would model '+(x.alternativeStaticHostingUSD===null?'a quote-required cost.':'$'+x.alternativeStaticHostingUSD.toFixed(2)+'/month, but requires a separate hosting decision.');
}
function snapshot(){return {exportedAt:new Date().toISOString(),scope:'manually entered review; not provider-verified',values:Object.fromEntries(all().map(e=>[e.id,e.type==='checkbox'?e.checked:e.value]))}}
try{const old=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('familyconnect-cost-review')||'null');if(old)for(const e of all())if(e.id in old.values){if(e.type==='checkbox')e.checked=old.values[e.id];else e.value=old.values[e.id]}}catch{}
for(const e of all())e.addEventListener('input',update);
document.getElementById('save').onclick=()=>{try{localStorage.setItem('familyconnect-cost-review',JSON.stringify(snapshot()));document.getElementById('saved').textContent='Saved in this browser only.'}catch{document.getElementById('saved').textContent='Browser storage unavailable; export JSON instead.'}};
document.getElementById('export').onclick=()=>{const a=document.createElement('a'),url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(snapshot(),null,2)],{type:'application/json'}));a.href=url;a.download='familyconnect-cost-review.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000)};
update();'''
Path('MONTHLY-COST-DASHBOARD.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>FamilyConnect monthly cost dashboard</title><style>'+styles+'</style><main>'+dashboard+'</main><script>'+script+'</script></html>',encoding='utf-8')
print('Built readiness report and monthly dashboard.')
